From 30b615826c72dc945e93ef975833d4e813cc0831 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:33:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 120/125] vless: VLESS Encryption of Xray for the outbound,
 with Vision over it

A server of Xray that has "decryption" set takes no client without this layer: a link
from the field (xhttp over REALITY, encryption=mlkem768x25519plus.native.0rtt.<key>)
passed with Xray 26.9.9 three times of three and with sing-box without the layer none.

The option "encryption" of a VLESS outbound takes the client's setting as Xray writes
it. The layer itself (protocol/vless/encryption: client.go, common.go, xor.go) is the
code of Xray-core v26.9.30 under its MPL-2.0 notice, with nothing changed but the imports
and three helpers; the server side is kept for the tests only. It sits between the
transport and VLESS, for TCP and UDP alike. Its handshake takes a bare connection and
nothing to end it by, so the connection is closed when the dial is cancelled or the
handshake has taken the time a TLS one is given.

Vision works on the layer as it does in Xray: the layer has the buffers Vision looks
for, and one entry in the list of sing-vmess is enough; a TLS connection under the
layer is not written past. So a flow is taken over any transport when the encryption is
set, where it is refused or warned about without.

Tests: the client against the server of Xray, every mode, both handshakes, both kinds
of key, two keys, an unknown ticket, the padding, a wrong key; the handshake against a
server that does not answer. Stand against Xray 26.9.9 (rs-lab/r14/enc): 55 cases.
